<title>POLAND: Warsaw bourse changes two stocks in WIG-20 index.</title>
<headline>Warsaw bourse changes two stocks in WIG-20 index.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Warsaw bourse added Animex and Optimus and withdrew Gorazdze and Rolimpex from the WIG-20 index of large-cap, high-volume stocks, a bourse official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Beata Mroz of the bourse's statistics department told Reuters that the new WIG 20, would be effective on January 16.</p>
<p>The other stocks of the WIG-20 include: Elektrim, Bank Slaski, BPH, BRE, WBK, BIG, Stomil, Wedel, Universal, Agros, Stalexport.</p>
<p>It also inscludes Mostostal Export, Okocim, Debica, Zywiec, Kety, Budimex and Polifarb Cieszyn.</p>
<p>The bourse updates the list quarterly.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
